# Declare line endings here instead of leaving them to each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Tooling that reads these files byte-for-byte breaks on a CRLF
# working tree — `git apply` on the llama patch, a shebang, a regex over
# Cargo.lock — and every such bug was invisible on macOS, where the working tree
# and the repo already agree. Every blob in this repo is LF today, so this
# changes no committed content; it only fixes what a Windows checkout writes to
# disk, and stops a CRLF blob from ever entering history.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Applied with `git apply` against an LF upstream checkout. The rule above
# already keeps it LF; -whitespace stops git flagging upstream's context lines.
vendor/llama.cpp/patches/*.patch -whitespace
